<p>The right website audit software is the product that can reproduce your site's important states and move verified findings into your team's workflow. Shortlist by task and constraints, then test the same representative URLs in each finalist. A vendor's issue count or health score is not a cross-product quality measure.</p>

<h2 id="what-makes-good-audit-software">What Makes Good Audit Software?</h2>

<p>Write a test brief before viewing plans. Include the largest crawl, JavaScript-rendered templates, authenticated or staging access, URL sources, required exports, team roles, integrations and monitoring frequency. Check whether the tool shows raw URL-level evidence behind each issue and lets you reproduce the result.</p>

<h2 id="ahrefs">Ahrefs Site Audit</h2>

<p><a href="https://ahrefs.com/site-audit" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ahrefs Site Audit</a> is a cloud crawler with predefined technical and on-page checks, JavaScript execution, configurable crawl controls, raw page and link explorers, exports and stored project history. It fits teams that also use Ahrefs' wider search data. Verified sites can use <a href="https://ahrefs.com/webmaster-tools" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ahrefs Free</a> within its current allowance.</p>

<h2 id="semrush">Semrush Site Audit</h2>

<p><a href="https://www.semrush.com/kb/31-site-audit" rel="noopener noreferrer">Semrush Site Audit</a> runs within a Semrush project and provides issue, crawlability, HTTPS, international SEO, Core Web Vitals and performance views. It suits teams that want audit evidence beside other Semrush modules. Page limits, project limits and rendering availability are plan-dependent.</p>

<h2 id="sitebulb">Sitebulb</h2>

<p><a href="https://sitebulb.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sitebulb</a> offers desktop and cloud crawling products with visualisations, issue guidance and crawl comparison. Assess the desktop or cloud option separately because deployment, collaboration and pricing differ.</p>

<h2 id="contentking">Conductor Website Monitoring</h2>

<p>ContentKing is now presented as <a href="https://www.conductor.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Conductor Website Monitoring</a>. Its distinct task is monitoring selected website conditions and changes between periodic deep audits. Confirm current coverage, alert routing, integrations and commercial terms with Conductor.</p>

<h2 id="lumar">Lumar</h2>

<p><a href="https://www.lumar.io/platform/technical-seo-metrics/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lumar</a> positions its platform for technical SEO analysis and monitoring at enterprise scale, with segmentation, custom metrics and workflow features. It is a sales-led option: use a proof of concept to test your site architecture, access needs and exports.</p>

<h2 id="deepcrawl">Deepcrawl Is Now Lumar</h2>

<p>Deepcrawl is not a separate current product to compare. <a href="https://www.lumar.io/meet-lumar-our-new-brand/" rel="noopener noreferrer">The company renamed Deepcrawl to Lumar in 2022</a>. Treat older Deepcrawl reviews and screenshots as historical unless Lumar's current documentation confirms the feature.</p>

<h2 id="our-recommendations">Choose with a Trial Script</h2>

<ol>
  <li>Crawl the same representative section with documented settings.</li>
  <li>Confirm discovery from links, sitemaps and any uploaded URL list.</li>
  <li>Compare raw and rendered HTML on a JavaScript-dependent template.</li>
  <li>Export one issue with every affected URL and hand it to the person who would fix it.</li>
  <li>Repeat after a known change and inspect crawl comparison or alert behaviour.</li>
  <li>Calculate cost at expected pages, projects, seats and crawl frequency from current vendor terms.</li>
</ol>

<p>If your team already works in Moz Pro, review the <a href="/website-audit-tools/moz/">Moz Site Crawl workflow</a>. A site owner who wants a guided first pass can assess <a href="/website-audit-tools/ubersuggest/">Ubersuggest Site Audit</a> against the same trial script.</p>

<p>For smaller or single-purpose checks, use the filters in our <a href="/website-audit-tools/">website audit tool directory</a>. For a three-tool deployment comparison, see <a href="/website-audit-tools/comparison/">Ahrefs vs Semrush vs Screaming Frog</a>.</p>

<p><small>Vendor facts checked against official product documentation on 11 September 2026.</small></p>

</ContentLayout>
